<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπᾰληθ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prove true, substantiate, verify,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν αἰτίαν, τὸν λόγον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.85
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				8.52
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργοις τὴν προσηγορίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					7.8.1
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.58
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>prove one's right to,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὔνομα, τὴν πρόσρησιν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				263
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>to be true, genuine,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαληθεῦον καὶ παγίως
			ἐνιδρυμένον</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				311
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				31
			</span></i> bis, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				10.17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τῷ ὀνόματι</span>
			<i>use</i> the name <i>correctly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				5.9.5
			</span></i>; <i>assert truly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dexipp.
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				50.24
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			); but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ γὰρ -εύει τῷ
				ἐξῃρημένῳ τὸ οἰκεῖον ὄνομα κατ᾽ ἀκρίβειαν</span>
			the transcendent <i>is</i> not strictly <i>entitled</i> to its
			own name, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				7
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
